      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-216081",
      ":question/problem": "Select the correct options in the truth table below and use this to determine whether $(X\u2227\u00acY)\u2227(X\u2228Y)$ is a contradiction.\n\n| $\\,X\\,$ | $\\,Y\\,$ | $\\,X\u2227\u00acY\\,$ | $\\,X\u2228Y\\,$ | $\\,(X\u2227\u00acY)\u2227(X\u2228Y)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-4}} |\n\nAccording to the table, $(X\u2227\u00acY)\u2227(X\u2228Y)$ \n{{field-5}}\nalways false. Therefore, it \n{{field-6}} \na contradiction."
    },
